Now read the benchmark order to see presentation order.

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "data/benchmark_order.json"
  }
}
```

Now run the script to see the data.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python explore.py"
  }
}
```

Also need to adjust load_benchmark path.

```json
{
  "tool": "edit_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "code/explore.py",
    "old_str": "def load_benchmark(code):\n    train = pd.read_csv(f\"data/{code}_train.csv\")\n    val = pd.read_csv(f\"data/{code}_val.csv\")\n    test = pd.read_csv(f\"data/{code}_test.csv\")\n    return train, val, test",
    "new_str": "def load_benchmark(code):\n    train = pd.read_csv(f\"../data/{code}_train.csv\")\n    val = pd.read_csv(f\"../data/{code}_val.csv\")\n    test = pd.read_csv(f\"../data/{code}_test.csv\")\n    return train, val, test"
  }
}
```

Now run again.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python explore.py"
  }
}
```

Run it.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python summarize_all.py"
  }
}
```

